## Known Brainstrike Issues & Workarounds

### Theme Toggle Limitation

When theme is `system`, the toggle logic sets to `light`. Prefer establishing a **known state** first, or emulate the system color scheme for deterministic tests.

```ts
test('theme toggle workaround', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Settings' }).click();
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Light' }).click();

  const themeToggle = page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Toggle theme' });
  await themeToggle.click();
  await expect(page.locator('html')).toHaveClass(/dark/);
});
```

> For truly system-level behavior, emulate color scheme via config (`use: { colorScheme: 'dark' }`) or `page.emulateMedia({ colorScheme: 'dark' })`.

### Page Reload Navigation Behavior

After reload, the app returns to Context Explorer:

```ts
test('reload behavior', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Settings' }).click();
  await page.reload();
  await expect(
  page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Context Explorer', exact: true })
    .and(page.locator('[aria-current="page"]'))
).toBeVisible();
});
```

