## Theme Testing Patterns

### Key Notes

* **System vs. DOM**: Your state may be `system`, but DOM actually has `light` or `dark`.
* **Deterministic tests**: Emulate color scheme in config or switch via `page.emulateMedia` and assert with `toHaveClass`.

### Common Failures & Fixes

```ts
// ❌ Avoid ambiguous text selectors
await expect(page.getByText('Theme')).toBeVisible();

// ✅ Use exact text or regex anchor
await expect(page.getByText(/^Theme$/)).toBeVisible();
```

```ts
// ❌ Don’t assume initial theme
await expect(page.locator('html')).not.toHaveClass(/dark/);

// ✅ Establish known state or emulate media
await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Settings' }).click();
await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Light' }).click();
await expect(page.locator('html')).not.toHaveClass(/dark/);
```

```ts
// ❌ Avoid sleep after toggle
await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Dark' }).click();
await page.waitForTimeout(100);

// ✅ Assert directly (auto-wait)
await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Dark' }).click();
await expect(page.locator('html')).toHaveClass(/dark/);
```

### Reliable Theme Testing

```ts
test('theme functionality', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Settings' }).click();

  // Known state
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Light' }).click();
  await expect(page.locator('html')).not.toHaveClass(/dark/);

  // Toggle
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Dark' }).click();
  await expect(page.locator('html')).toHaveClass(/dark/);

  // Persists across navigation
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Context Explorer' }).click();
  await expect(page.locator('html')).toHaveClass(/dark/);
});
```

